    "note": "Float64 re-run of data/batch/2026-11-14 certainty_height + certainty_height_fine (polaris_batch v2). The original run held terrain heights in float32, so R + h (R = 1,737,400 m) was rounded to about 0.125 m and the ray elevation angles carried that error (LONG_FEATURES_2026-11-15 section 0). Run with float32 heights, this script reproduces the original summary to within 0.001 points (same definitions: 720 bins at (k+0.5)*0.5 deg, linear interpolation between bins, near 1 m steps to 25 km, far 80 m to 280 km, h0 = z0 + mast, Sun/Earth centre vs horizon, the bundle's 337 hourly Horizons samples 2026-11-14 00:00 to 2026-11-28 00:00 UTC). Only the precision changes. Site01 ROI6: identical to the original. Site04 ROI3: masts 1-1.75 m change (1 m Sun nominal 93.769 -> 94.362 = the repo bundle's 318/337; clone values shift by up to 1.8 points); 2 m and above identical. Certainty Height, agreement mast and pass counts are unchanged. Columns: only the two metrics the viewer reads (sun_centre_pct, both_centre_pct); sun_disc, earth_any and gap metrics were not re-run. The original folder is untouched.",
